drm/virtio: add the blob_alignment parameter (hosts with larger pages)

Problem. libkrun on Apple silicon maps host-visible blob resources into the
guest's "host window" with Hypervisor.framework, whose mapping granule is the
host page size (16 KiB). A guest with 4 KiB pages must therefore create
host3d blobs whose size is a multiple of 16 KiB, and place them at 16 KiB
aligned offsets of the window. Otherwise the host cannot map them (hv_vm_map
fails and the blob map command returns an error) and Vulkan instance creation
fails in the guest.

Userspace (Mesa Venus, 26.2.4 and later) already queries
VIRTGPU_PARAM_BLOB_ALIGNMENT (9) and pads its blob sizes to the value it
gets. Mainline kernels do not implement the parameter.

What this patch does:

 - adds the module parameter virtio_gpu.blob_alignment: unsigned int, a power
   of two, default 0 meaning "no constraint", read-only after boot (mode
   0400). The VMM or launcher sets it on the kernel command line, for libkrun
   on Apple silicon: virtio_gpu.blob_alignment=16384. The driver is built in,
   so the command-line prefix is the driver name, virtio_gpu.
 - DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_GETPARAM(VIRTGPU_PARAM_BLOB_ALIGNMENT) returns it (new
   uapi define, value 9).
 - RESOURCE_CREATE_BLOB for host3d blobs (blobs without guest memory) whose
   size is not a multiple of the alignment is rejected with EINVAL. A value
   that is not a power of two rejects all such blobs.
 - the placement of host-visible blobs in the host window honours the
   alignment (drm_mm_insert_node_generic() with that alignment).

With the parameter at its default of 0 the behaviour is exactly that of
mainline.

Written against linux-6.18.56, the kernel pinned by vmapp (kernel/pins.env).
It is applied by kernel/build.sh --flavour gpu to the verified source tree
with patch -p1 --fuzz=0, and only in that flavour. The default vmapp kernel
has no DRM at all and does not contain it.

